                <pb facs="0260" n="890" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg890"/>

                <head>No. 389.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Received Feb. 13—4.15 p.m.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 13,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of 12th received. Conference with Castelar
                    appointed for 4 this afternoon; time and manner of presentation to President of
                    republic will then be arranged.</p>
                <p>Martos, who declined the presidency of the republic, was
                    last night elected president of the sovereign assembly.</p>
                <p>Tranquillity uninterrupted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>SICKLES.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
